{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And they gathered it morning by morning.</b> 'Morning' — two hours, and 'morning' — two hours, making four hours; and from four hours onward the sun grew warm and it melted. And they would distribute it in the manner of charity to anyone who neglected and did not gather in the morning. And a great miracle was performed through the manna: just as a prophet would tell hidden things, so the manna, when a slave fled and was found in the possession of another — this one says, 'You sold him to me,' and that one says, 'He fled from me' — if his omer was found in the house of his original master, it is known that he fled; and if it was found in the house of the other, where he is, it is known that the first one sold him. And likewise a woman who fled from her husband's house — she says, 'He transgressed against me,' and he says, 'She transgressed against me.' Moses our master said to them: 'In the morning, judgment.' The next day, if the omer was found in her husband's house, it is known that she transgressed against him; if the omer was found in her father's house, it is known that he transgressed against her and he had put her out of his house. Thus did our Rabbis of blessed memory expound in tractate Yoma. Scripture alludes to this by כזרע גד — 'like coriander seed' — for the manna would tell Israel hidden matters and many laws and judgments."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:00:08.518427142Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}